#  Example of input file for utility makemol
#  Create .mmol file for DMPC lipid with Slipids force field
#  Simple molecular file (.smol) should already exist (prepared by other tools)
#
#  Force field file
Slipids-c36.ff
#  simple molecular file .smol / .crd / .alc : 
dmpc.smol
# Format of the input file:
#  0 - default (Xmol - like: .smol)
#  1 - CHARMM-like (.crd)
#  2 - Alchemy-like (.alc)
0
#  Include Urey-Bradley term?  (0/1)
1
#  Skip writing of non-present angles in .mmol?  (0/1)
0
#  Output .mmol file
dmpc.mmol
#
#  Log will be written in makemol.log
